---
import data from "../data/site-data.json";
import { gh, num, pct } from "./format";

const h = data.nsfg.headline.all;
const cal = Object.fromEntries(data.nlsy.calibration.map((c) => [c.range_pct, c]));
const logit = data.nsfg.model.holdout.find((m) => m.model === "logistic")!;
const prim = data.m10.primary.find((p) => p.role === "primary")!;
const f2040 = data.m11.forecast[data.m11.forecast.length - 1];
const e = Object.fromEntries(data.m11.endpoints.map((x) => [x.c, x]));
---
<section class="section conclusion" id="conclusion" aria-labelledby="ch5">
  <header class="conclusion-opening">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div class="conclusion-meta c-1-4">
        <span class="conclusion-label">Conclusion</span>
        <span class="conclusion-code">Synthesis · frozen November 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="conclusion-title c-4-13" id="ch5">Whether Generation Z will have the families it wants cannot be established from the existing data.</h2>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap conclusion-evidence">
    <div class="grid conclusion-context">
      <p class="standfirst c-4-13">
        A population-level answer would need two things no source provides: a numeric desired family size for Generation Z, and the completed
        lifetime fertility of the same cohorts. An answer about individuals would also need the same people followed over time. What the evidence does
        support is a set of separate, bounded statements. None of them is a measured gap between desire and achievement.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="conclusion-ledger">
      <div>
        <h3>What the evidence supports</h3>
        <ol class="ledger-list">
          <li>In 2022–23, {pct(h.wants.est)} of U.S. adults aged about 18–27 wanted a child or another child, and {pct(h.intends.est)} intended one.
            <span class="kind">Stated desire and intention · weighted survey · strong</span></li>
          <li>Of those who wanted a child, {pct(h.divergence_among_wanters.est)} did not intend one; about {Math.round((h.sterility_among_wanters.est / h.divergence_among_wanters.est) * 100)}% of that was the survey's sterility classification. Demographic models could not predict the explicit &ldquo;no&rdquo; on unseen data (AUC {num(logit.auc, 2)} against 0.50).
            <span class="kind">Stated intention · negative machine-learning result · strong</span></li>
          <li>In an earlier cohort, women born 1980–84, stated chances of a birth ranked the outcomes (AUC {num(data.nlsy.forecast.auc, 3)}) but were far too extreme: {num(cal["0"].observed_pct)}% of those who said 0% had a birth, and {num(cal["100"].observed_pct)}% of those who said 100%.
            <span class="kind">Expectations against observed births · unweighted · strong for that cohort, untested for Generation Z</span></li>
          <li>Rent burden was not robustly associated with state birth rates: {num(prim.est, 2)} per 10 points at ages 20–24 (95% interval {num(prim.lo, 2)} to {num(prim.hi, 2)}), and none at 25–29.
            <span class="kind">Ecological association · not causal</span></li>
          <li>The 2040 U.S. total fertility rate forecast is the 2024 level, {num(f2040.f, 3)}. Its range failed calibration, so there is no reliable directional signal.
            <span class="kind">Model forecast · moderate</span></li>
          <li>If 2024 rates persist, women born in 1995 reach about {num(e[1995].p2040, 2)} births by the end of 2040, nearly complete; women born in 2012 reach about {num(e[2012].p2040, 2)}, far from complete.
            <span class="kind">Conditional projection · not completed fertility</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="conclusion-companion">
        <div>
        <h3>What must not be inferred</h3>
        <ol class="ledger-list not">
          <li><strong>A gap, by subtraction.</strong> Survey answers and projected cohort fertility describe different people, measures and times.</li>
          <li><strong>Probabilities from the forecast ranges.</strong> They are ranges built from past errors, and they failed calibration.</li>
          <li><strong>Completed family size from the projections.</strong> No projection to 2040 is completed lifetime fertility; those for people born after 2002 are far from it.</li>
          <li><strong>Causes from the housing results.</strong> They are associations between states and years.</li>
          <li><strong>Population estimates from the NLSY97 results.</strong> They are unweighted results for one earlier cohort.</li>
        </ol>
        </div>
        <div class="conclusion-future">
          <h3>What would answer the question</h3>
          <ol class="ledger-list">
            <li>A numeric desired family-size question asked of Generation Z.</li>
            <li>Following the same respondents until their childbearing years end, around age 45.</li>
            <li>Forecasts whose probability intervals pass a calibration check.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="further">
      <a href={gh("docs/final_executive_summary.md")}>Executive summary</a>
      <a href={gh("docs/final_synthesis_manuscript.md")}>Integrated manuscript</a>
      <a href={gh("docs/final_claim_evidence_matrix.csv")}>Claim-to-evidence matrix</a>
      <a href={gh("docs/final_limitations_register.md")}>Limitations register</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section.conclusion {
    padding-block: 0;
  }

  .conclusion-opening {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7.7vw, 7.5rem);
    background: #20201f;
    color: var(--paper-light);
  }

  .conclusion-opening::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    z-index: -1;
    inset: 0 0 0 67%;
    border-inline-start: 1px solid #403c37;
    background: var(--ink);
  }

  .conclusion-opening .grid {
    align-items: start;
    row-gap: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .conclusion-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }

  .conclusion-meta::before {
    content: "";
    inline-size: 2.5rem;
    block-size: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--oxblood-soft);
  }

  .conclusion-label {
    color: var(--paper);
    font: 500 clamp(1.4rem, 1.1rem + 0.65vw, 2rem)/1.1 var(--serif);
  }

  .conclusion-code {
    color: #c9baa8;
    font: 400 0.78rem/1.5 var(--mono);
  }

  .conclusion-title {
    max-width: 24ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 1.3rem + 3.8vw, 4.85rem);
    font-weight: 390;
    line-height: 1.02;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 60;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .conclusion-evidence {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem) clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .conclusion-context {
    margin-block-end: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .conclusion-context .standfirst {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1.75rem);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--oxblood);
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 0.98rem + 0.55vw, 1.38rem);
  }

  .conclusion-ledger {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.75rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .conclusion-companion {
    display: grid;
    align-content: start;
    gap: clamp(2.75rem, 5.5vw, 4.75rem);
  }

  .conclusion-ledger h3 {
    margin-block-end: clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.25rem + 1.45vw, 2.7rem);
    font-weight: 440;
    line-height: 1.08;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .conclusion-ledger li {
    padding-block: clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
    padding-inline-start: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  .conclusion-ledger li::before {
    top: clamp(0.85rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem);
  }

  .conclusion-ledger li:first-child {
    border-top-color: var(--ink);
  }

  .conclusion-ledger .kind {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .conclusion-future {
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--oxblood);
    background: var(--paper-light);
  }

  .conclusion-future li:last-child {
    padding-block-end: 0;
  }

  .conclusion-evidence .further {
    margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 60em) {
    .conclusion-ledger {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .conclusion-meta {
      padding-top: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media print {
    .conclusion-opening {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    .conclusion-opening::after {
      display: none;
    }

    .conclusion-label,
    .conclusion-code {
      color: var(--ink);
    }
  }
</style>
